ATTRIBUTION AND PROVENANCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MRound is an independent reimplementation of the SignRound and SignRound v2
weight-only quantization methods, written for Apple Silicon from the published
descriptions of those methods. It is not a fork of, and contains no source code
copied from, any prior implementation.

MRound implements methods described in the following publications:

1. Cheng, W., Zhang, W., Shen, H., Cai, Y., He, X., Lv, K., Liu, Y.
   "Optimize Weight Rounding via Signed Gradient Descent for the Quantization
   of LLMs." arXiv:2309.05516. Published at EMNLP 2024 (Findings).
   https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.05516

2. Cheng, W., Zhang, W., Guo, H., Shen, H., Ma, Z.
   "SignRoundV2: Toward Closing the Performance Gap in Extremely Low-Bit
   Post-Training Quantization for LLMs." arXiv:2512.04746.
   https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.04746

The reference implementation of these methods is Intel AutoRound
(https://github.com/intel/auto-round), Copyright Intel Corporation, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

MRound uses Intel AutoRound as a behavioral reference and numerical parity
oracle during development and testing. Where MRound must interoperate with
formats that AutoRound defines or consumes, MRound implements those formats from
their observable on-disk structure and copies no source code from any
implementation of them.

Any file in this repository that does incorporate code from a third-party
Apache-2.0 project carries, in its own header, the original copyright line, the
upstream project name, and a statement of what was changed, as required by
Section 4 of the License. The authoritative list of such files is maintained in
THIRD_PARTY_ATTRIBUTIONS.md. If that file is absent or empty, no third-party
code is present in this repository.


